From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 11:46:25 +0200
Subject: Treat non-specialized anonymous-class parents as such, not as a crash
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Specialization.anonymousClassIsSpecialized matches any parent call with two
argument lists (Apply(Apply(t, args), ev)) and then unconditionally does
Specialization.unapply(...).get — but that shape also arises for an ordinary
parent whose constructor takes a second (e.g. using) argument list, where the
parent type is no AppliedType and the unapply returns None, so the compiler
crashes with NoSuchElementException in FirstTransform. Seven-line flagless
reproduction:

    class Base(x: Int)(using s: String)
    given String = "ctx"
    inline def make(): Base = new Base(1) {}
    @main def crash() = println(make())

None simply means the parent is not a specialized trait; answer false.
Introduced upstream by #26156 (Inline Traits & Specialized Traits). Upstream
#26842 has since removed the .get, but its `.map(_.hasSpecializedParams).nonEmpty`
is just `isDefined`: any specialization candidate counts, whether or not it has
specialized params. This patch keeps the original predicate,
`exists(_.hasSpecializedParams)`; upstream candidate.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: anonspec
---
 .../dotc/transform/DesugarSpecializedTraits.scala      | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/DesugarSpecializedTraits.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/DesugarSpecializedTraits.scala
index 9598d36e0f0b953e555848c7c5757b13db238a1f..0bcf56213ffcd544bb8c78578dd31a89c1f8d4dd 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/DesugarSpecializedTraits.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/transform/DesugarSpecializedTraits.scala
@@ -854,10 +854,12 @@ object Specialization:
       case TypeDef(anon, Template(_, parentCalls: List[Tree], _, _)) =>
         parentCalls match {
           case _ :+ Apply(Apply(t, ctorArgs), ev) => // extends Object, parents of spec trait, spec trait
-            Specialization
-              .unapply(t.tpe.resultType.resultType, t.span)
-              .map(_.hasSpecializedParams)
-              .nonEmpty
+            // A two-Apply parent call also arises for any ordinary parent whose
+            // constructor takes a second (e.g. using) argument list; its type is
+            // then no AppliedType and the unapply returns None, meaning "not a
+            // specialized trait" — not a crash.
+            val spec = Specialization.unapply(t.tpe.resultType.resultType, t.span)
+            spec.exists(_.hasSpecializedParams)
           case _ => false
         }
       case _ => false
